# Copy to .env.local for the local preview, and set the same names in the
# Vercel project environment for the deployed build. Never commit .env.local.

# YouTube Data API v3. Without it the app falls back to oEmbed, which gives
# a title and a channel but no duration or upload date.
YOUTUBE_API_KEY=

# Google Drive sync. Both of these are PUBLIC identifiers: they reach the
# browser, and /api/config hands them over on request. They live here so the
# repository carries no credentials, not because they are secret.
#
# What actually protects them is in the Google Cloud console:
#   - GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID: add your deployed origin and http://localhost:3000
#     to the OAuth client's Authorized JavaScript origins.
#   - GOOGLE_API_KEY: restrict it to those same HTTP referrers, and to the
#     Google Picker API only.
#
# The OAuth client SECRET is deliberately absent. The browser-only token flow
# never uses one, so there is no secret for this project to leak.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_API_KEY=
